                                "sense_id": "2358a4a0-ba7f-39a5-9e16-a4fb9d0e4d67",
                                "text": "It used to be the fashion to put a second thick covering or \"pilch\" over the napkin to keep the outer clothes from wet; but this is by no means healthy, as it over-heats this part of the body, and is often a mere excuse for neglecting the frequent changes that should be made, so that the skin is apt to become sodden, and subsequently sore, from damp heat."
